      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, you should test your home's indoor air quality with a comprehensive kit before attempting any filtering, as the symptoms described could indicate VOCs or poor ventilation rather than the mist itself. Once confirmed, focus on sealing leaks to prevent water spray from re-entering the home while upgrading to high-quality heating and cooling units rather than standalone air purifiers for this level of contamination. Consult a local environmental health agency for guidance on tracking the source and preventing future utility conflicts with your neighbor.",
