    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the air quality kit showed some spikes in organic compounds right when the neighbor's misting system hits, so it's definitely not just my imagination. it's getting harder to breathe when the wind blows toward my windows. i can't just seal the windows forever, i need to know if there are specific types of carbon filters or maybe even some kind of neutralizer i can set up near the vents to stop these particles before they actually get inside the house. what's most effective for heavy organic aerosols?",
