      "content": "For heavy organic aerosols, standard carbon filters alone are often insufficient because they lack thermal or biocidal power to neutralize volatile compounds like VOCs and mold; instead, you should prioritize a unit equipped with both an HEPA filter and an activated charcoal pre-filter capable of adsorption. Placing such a system on a high intake intake on negative pressure side of your ventilation to create a protective filter wall is crucial, but remember that only 40% of pollution is removed this way. For immediate relief, considering a dedicated UVGI lamp on the intake or engaging your local environmental health board for proven solutions is often more effective than DIY home remedies.",
